-- examples/flag/flag.rofl — A PROPOSITION IS A RELATION OF ARITY ZERO.
--
-- The capability added 2026-09-10, exercised on a demo's real path because
-- CLAUDE.md is right that nothing else can see it: a grammar production that
-- nothing uses cannot go red.
--
-- WHAT A NULLARY RELATION IS. A relation of arity n is a set of n-TUPLES.
-- There is exactly ONE 0-tuple, the empty one, so a nullary relation's
-- extension is either the empty set or that singleton — it is a TRUTH VALUE.
-- `deploy_blocked()` is not "a relation to nothing"; it is a proposition, and
-- propositional logic is the base case of the predicate logic this language
-- already was.

-- The world: three services, two of them healthy.
service(auth).
service(billing).
service(search).
healthy(auth).
healthy(billing).

-- THE PROPOSITION. One rule, one row, no subject — and the subject it does
-- not need is supplied by the BOOK it lives in, which is what perspectives
-- are for. `in whose book is this entry` answers: in `main`'s.
deploy_blocked() :- service(S), not healthy(S).

-- WHAT IT BUYS, and it is the whole point. Before nullary heads this had to
-- be written `blocked(S) :- service(S), unhealthy_somewhere(_).` — a variable
-- carried only so the head had something to name, re-derived once per
-- service, and a cross product against the whole unhealthy set. Now the guard
-- is ONE ROW and the join against it is a constant.
releasable(S) :- service(S), not deploy_blocked().

-- ...AND THE NEGATION SAYS WHAT IT READS. `not deploy_blocked()` is
-- "nothing blocks the deploy". Written the old way, `not blocked(S)` reads as
-- "this S is not blocked" and MEANS the global thing only because the dummy
-- variable made the relation uniform — a fact the author had to prove and the
-- reader had to trust. Here there is nothing to prove.

-- TWO BOOKS, TWO PROPOSITIONS. The same name in two ledgers is two different
-- truths, which is the answer to "a fact must be ABOUT something": a
-- proposition is about the book it is in.
frozen[prod]().
ship[prod](S)  :- service(S), not frozen[prod]().
ship[stage](S) :- service(S), not frozen[stage]().
